- content_for :title, "Membership | Cragmont Climbing Club"
- content_for :body_class, "club-page"
= render "shared/public_header"
%main.public-main.club-main
  %article.panel.club-panel
    %p.eyebrow Cragmont Climbing Club
    %h1 Membership
    = render "navigation"
    .club-copy.content-page-markdown
      %p.club-lead You do not have to climb the hardest grade to belong here. Knowing your limits, climbing thoughtfully, and contributing to the community matter more.
      %h2 The path to membership
      %ol.club-requirements
        %li
          %strong Climb with the club.
          Spend time on a club trip with at least one member. A signed liability release is required before participating in club climbing.
        %li
          %strong Use sound judgment.
          Be honest about your experience, understand what you do and do not know, and make safe decisions with your partners. A membership recommendation is not a certification of climbing ability.
        %li
          %strong Take part.
          Get to know the people and the club. Members help make trips and events happen, from organizing outings to arranging campsites.
        %li
          %strong Ask for recommendations.
          Once you are ready, two members who have climbed with you can recommend you. Membership is then discussed at a club business meeting; the time this takes varies from person to person.
      %h2 Getting started
      %p Join the email list, introduce yourself, and come to a local gathering or a trip that fits your experience. Climb with different members over time and ask questions about the membership process. Full membership does not mean someone is able to lead every route, so always discuss plans and skills with a prospective partner.
      .club-actions
        = link_to "Join the email list", join_the_list_path, class: "button"
        = link_to "See upcoming trips", trips_path, class: "button secondary"
